#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:3
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Konfiguracja"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:10
msgid "Project config file"
msgstr "Plik konfiguracji projektu"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:12
msgid ""
"Snapper looks for ``.snapperrc.toml`` starting from the current directory "
"and walking up to the filesystem root. Override the search with ``--config "
"path/to/config.toml``."
msgstr ""
"Snapper szuka pliku ``.snapperrc.toml`` począwszy od bieżącego katalogu w "
"górę aż do korzenia systemu plików. Przesłoń wyszukiwanie za pomocą ``--"
"config path/to/config.toml``."

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:15
msgid "Or generate one with ``snapper init``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:20
msgid "Config format"
msgstr "Format konfiguracji"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:73
msgid "Fields"
msgstr "Pola"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:78
msgid "lang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:80
msgid ""
"String. Language code for the built-in abbreviation set used by the rule-"
"based splitter. One of: ``en`` (default), ``de``, ``fr``, ``is``, ``pl``. "
"Also selectable via ``--lang`` CLI flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:88
msgid "extra\\ :sub:`abbreviations`"
msgstr "extra\\ :sub:`abbreviations`"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:90
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"String array. Each entry names an abbreviation that should not trigger a "
"sentence break when followed by a period. Merged with the built-in list for "
"the selected language. Useful for domain-specific terms your papers use "
"frequently."
msgstr ""
"Tablica ciągów znaków. Każdy wpis określa skrót, który nie powinien "
"powodować podziału zdania po kropce. Przydatne dla terminów dziedzinowych "
"często używanych w artykułach."

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:98
msgid "ignore"
msgstr "ignore"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:100
msgid ""
"String array of glob patterns. Files matching these patterns get skipped "
"during ``--in-place`` and ``--check`` operations. Does not affect stdin/"
"stdout mode."
msgstr ""
"Tablica ciągów znaków ze wzorcami glob. Pliki pasujące do tych wzorców są "
"pomijane podczas operacji ``--in-place`` i ``--check``. Nie wpływa na tryb "
"stdin/stdout."

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:107
msgid "format"
msgstr "format"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:109
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"String. Default format when auto-detection from file extension does not "
"apply. One of: ``org``, ``latex``, ``markdown``, ``rst``, ``plaintext``."
msgstr ""
"Ciąg znaków. Domyślny format, gdy automatyczne wykrywanie na podstawie "
"rozszerzenia pliku nie ma zastosowania. Jeden z: ``org``, ``latex``, "
"``markdown``, ``plaintext``."

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:116
msgid "max\\ :sub:`width`"
msgstr "max\\ :sub:`width`"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:118
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Integer. Sentences exceeding this width get wrapped at word boundaries. Set "
"to ``0`` for unlimited (the default). Also respects ``max_line_length`` from "
"``.editorconfig`` if present."
msgstr ""
"Liczba całkowita. Zdania przekraczające tę szerokość są zawijane na "
"granicach słów. Ustaw na ``0`` dla braku limitu (wartość domyślna)."

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:126
#, fuzzy
msgid "clause\\ :sub:`breaks`"
msgstr "extra\\ :sub:`abbreviations`"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:128
msgid "Boolean. Default: ``false``. Also selectable via ``--clause-breaks``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:132
msgid ""
"When true, snapper inserts a soft break after independent-clause punctuation "
"(comma, semicolon, colon, em dash, or ASCII ``--``) that is already followed "
"by whitespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:134
msgid ""
"``max_width = 0`` (the default): every such mark starts a new line. A "
"sentence that is already one independent clause stays one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:137
msgid ""
"``max_width > 0``: overflowing sentences prefer those marks; a sentence that "
"already fits stays on one line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:139
msgid ""
"Tokens such as ``1,000``, ``10:30``, URLs, ``--flags``, and unspaced dashes "
"never split. ``--check`` uses the same mode when this flag or config is on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:145
msgid "long\\ :sub:`threshold`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:147
msgid ""
"Integer. Character threshold for advisory ``long`` diagnostics when "
"``max_width`` is unset. Default: 120. A ``long`` finding is never the sole "
"cause of ``--check`` exit 1 unless ``--strict-long`` is set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:155
msgid "Per-format sections"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:157
msgid ""
"Add ``[org]``, ``[latex]``, ``[markdown]``, ``[rst]``, or ``[plaintext]`` "
"sections to override settings for specific formats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:159
msgid ""
"Per-format ``extra_abbreviations`` merge with the top-level list. Per-format "
"``max_width`` overrides the top-level value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:162
msgid ""
"The following keys are meaningful under ``[latex]`` only. Missing keys (or "
"empty arrays) keep the built-in lists; present entries are added to those "
"lists. There is no regex ``other:`` key (latexindent's pattern-based extra "
"matching is not supported)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:169
msgid "verbatim\\ :sub:`envs`\\ (latex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:171
msgid ""
"String array of environment names treated like ``minted`` / ``lstlisting`` / "
"``verbatim`` (``Region::Code``, no reflow). Built-in: ``minted``, "
"``lstlisting``, ``verbatim``. Adding ``Verbatim`` (fancyvrb) stops reflow of "
"that environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:178
msgid "structure\\ :sub:`envs`\\ (latex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:180
msgid ""
"String array of environment names treated like ``equation`` / ``figure`` "
"(``Region::Structure``, no reflow). Built-in: the ``NON_PROSE_ENVS`` list "
"(equation, align, figure, table, tabular, tikzpicture, and starred variants, "
"plus the built-in code envs). Adding ``algorithm`` or ``comment`` stops "
"reflow of those environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:187
msgid "verbatim\\ :sub:`commands`\\ (latex)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:189
msgid ""
"String array of extra command names tokenized like the built-in verb command "
"before sentence split. The next character after the name is the delimiter. "
"Built-in names are ``verb`` and ``lstinline``; ``lstinline`` still accepts "
"optional ``[...]`` and ``{...}``. Adding ``Verb`` (fancyvrb) keeps that "
"command's delimited body atomic and treats an inner ``%`` as content, not a "
"comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:197
msgid "Code-block sections (``[code.<lang>]``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:199
msgid ""
"Each ``[code.<lang>]`` table configures how fenced or delimited source "
"blocks for that language are handled. ``snapper init`` writes seed entries "
"for common languages (``rust``, ``python``, ``toml``, ``lua``, ``lisp``, "
"``html``, ``javascript``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:205
msgid "line\\ :sub:`comment`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:207
msgid ""
"String. Marker for single-line comments (for example ``\"//\"`` or "
"``\"#\"``). Comment text after the marker is reflowed with the sentence "
"splitter; the marker and indentation are preserved."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:211
msgid ""
"A marker that repeats or decorates this one keeps its written form, so ``///"
"`` and ``//!`` survive a split instead of collapsing to ``//``. A ``#!`` "
"shebang is left alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:214
msgid ""
"Where a grammar backs the language (see `grammar-backed-languages`_), the "
"reflow also reaches a comment that follows code on the same line, aligning "
"continuation sentences under the comment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:221
msgid ""
"Without a grammar the marker must open the line. That rule keeps the ``//`` "
"inside ``\"// not a comment.\"`` out of the reflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:227
msgid "block\\ :sub:`comment`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:229
msgid ""
"String array of length two: open and close markers (for example ``[\"/*\", "
"\"*/\"]``). One-line and multi-line block comments are reflowed as prose "
"between the markers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:235
msgid "string\\ :sub:`delims`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:237
msgid "String array of quote characters. Defaults to ``[\"\\\"\", \"'\"]``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:240
msgid ""
"Without a grammar, quoting is the only thing separating a comment marker "
"from the same characters inside a literal: a marker that trails code "
"reflows, while the same marker inside a quoted string does not. The tracking "
"stays conservative: an unbalanced quote, such as a Rust lifetime or an "
"apostrophe in a shell word, makes the rest of the line read as quoted, so a "
"marker after it goes unreflowed rather than mangled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:243
msgid ""
"Grammar-backed languages ignore this field; the parse already knows which "
"bytes belong to a string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:248
msgid "escape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:250
msgid ""
"String holding one character that escapes the next inside a string literal. "
"Defaults to a backslash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:256
#, fuzzy
msgid "formatter"
msgstr "format"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:258
msgid ""
"String array treated as argv for ``std::process::Command``. Only runs when "
"the CLI flag ``--format-code`` is set. Missing binaries, non-zero exits, and "
"a ~30s watchdog timeout each leave the reflowed body in place (non-fatal)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:262
msgid ""
"If a language has no ``[code.<lang>]`` entry (or the fence has no language), "
"the block body passes through unchanged aside from normal trailing-newline "
"preservation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:267
msgid "Grammar-backed languages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:269
msgid ""
"The ``treesitter`` feature, on by default, parses code blocks in ``rust``, "
"``python``, ``javascript``, ``c``, ``cpp``, ``go``, ``bash`` and ``html`` to "
"tell a comment from a string. Fence aliases resolve as well: ``rs``, ``py``, "
"``js``, ``sh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:272
msgid ""
"A build feature governs this, not a config field, and a ``[code.<lang>]`` "
"entry remains required. The grammar decides which bytes form a comment; the "
"entry supplies the markers used to re-emit it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:275
msgid ""
"Two builds carry no grammars and fall back to the scanner for every language:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:277
msgid ""
"``wasm32-unknown-unknown``, the target behind the Obsidian and Word "
"integrations, where the C runtime and its grammars would need a ``wasm`` "
"libc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:279
msgid ""
"Any build configured with ``--no-default-features`` that does not opt back "
"in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:281
msgid ""
"The VS Code extension runs the CLI rather than the wasm build, so it has "
"grammars."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:283
msgid ""
"The scanner reads `field-string-delims`_ to find trailing comments on its "
"own, so both engines agree on ordinary code. A grammar still wins on raw "
"strings, heredocs, triple-quoted strings and nested comments, where quote "
"counting alone gives the wrong answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:286
msgid ""
"Block comments stay on the scanner. A close marker inside a string does not "
"end the comment, so ``let s = \"*/\";`` in a ``/* ... */`` block stays in "
"the comment. When the closer is itself a quote sequence (``\"\"\"``, "
"``'''``), the first match is the closer, which is how Python docstrings "
"reflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:293
msgid "Precedence"
msgstr "Kolejność priorytetów"

#: ../../source/reference/config.rst:295
msgid ""
"CLI flags override config file values. Per-format sections override top-"
"level config values. Config file values override ``.editorconfig`` values. "
"``.editorconfig`` overrides built-in defaults."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid ""
#~ "CLI flags override config file values. Config file values override built-"
#~ "in defaults. Explicitly passing ``--format`` or ``--max-width`` always "
#~ "wins."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Flagi CLI nadpisują wartości z pliku konfiguracyjnego. Wartości z pliku "
